# conservation-tension-engine

A Python library implementing the **conservation of tension** principle from music theory research — measuring harmonic tension, tracking its conservation across chord progressions, and detecting violations.

## Install

```bash
pip install conservation-tension-engine
```

## Quick Start

```python
from conservation_tension import Pitch, Chord, TensionMeter, ChordProgression

# Work with pitches
p = Pitch.from_name("A4")
print(p.frequency)  # 440.0

# Parse and analyze chords
c = Chord.parse("Cmaj7")
print(c.quality)            # "maj7"
print(c.tension())          # spectral tension

# Compare tensions
major = Chord.parse("C")
dom7  = Chord.parse("G7")
print(TensionMeter.spectral_tension(major))   # lower
print(TensionMeter.spectral_tension(dom7))    # higher

# Analyze a full progression
prog = ChordProgression(["Cmaj7", "Dm7", "G7", "Cmaj7"])
analysis = prog.analyze(key="C")
print(analysis.tension_curve)         # per-chord tension
print(analysis.conservation_score)    # 0-1 smoothness score
print(analysis.cadences)              # detected cadences (ii-V-I, V-I)
```

## API Overview

### Pitch
- `Pitch.from_name("C4")` / `Pitch.from_midi(60)` — construct from name or MIDI
- `pitch.interval_to(other)` — interval in cents
- `pitch.harmonics(n=8)` — overtone series as frequencies

### Chord
- `Chord.parse("Cmaj7")` — parse standard chord symbols
- `chord.quality` — detected quality (major, minor, dom7, maj7, etc.)
- `chord.tension(method="spectral")` — compute harmonic tension

### TensionMeter
- `spectral_tension(chord)` — distance from pure harmonic series
- `voice_leading_tension(prev, curr)` — minimal voice-leading distance
- `contextual_tension(chord, key)` — distance from tonal center

### ConservationLaw
- `check(tensions)` — full conservation analysis
- `violations(tensions)` — indices where tension jumps exceed threshold
- `tension_budget(tensions)` — total, average, variance, budget used

### MeantoneComparison
- `meantone_fifth(ratio=5/4)` — compute meantone fifth size
- `compare_tension(chord)` — meantone vs equal temperament
- `wolf_interval("quarter-comma")` — size of the wolf interval

### ChordProgression
- `analyze()` — full analysis with tension curve, conservation, cadences, key areas
- `conservation_score()` — 0–1 smoothness measure
- `cadences()` — detect ii-V-I, V-I patterns

